    {id="original-star-100",subject="Reading / ELA",skill="Details",prompt="Read the passage: A robin carried twigs to a tree. It tucked grass between the twigs. Soon a small round nest rested on a branch. The nest would be a place for the robin to lay its eggs. What did the robin tuck between the twigs?",answer="Grass",hint="Reread the passage and look for words that support your answer.",explanation="The second sentence says it tucked grass between the twigs.",choices={"Stones","Snow","Paper cups","Grass"},tier="star-fallback",sourceFact="Original Grade 2 STAR-style practice",provenance={["kind"]="original-star-style"},priority=1},
    {id="original-star-101",subject="Reading / ELA",skill="Purpose",prompt="Read the passage: A robin carried twigs to a tree. It tucked grass between the twigs. Soon a small round nest rested on a branch. The nest would be a place for the robin to lay its eggs. Why did the robin build the nest?",answer="To have a place for its eggs",hint="Reread the passage and look for words that support your answer.",explanation="The last sentence explains the purpose.",choices={"To have a place for its eggs","To store shoes","To hide a bicycle","To catch fish"},tier="star-fallback",sourceFact="Original Grade 2 STAR-style practice",provenance={["kind"]="original-star-style"},priority=1},
    {id="original-star-102",subject="Reading / ELA",skill="Vocabulary",prompt="Read the passage: A robin carried twigs to a tree. It tucked grass between the twigs. Soon a small round nest rested on a branch. The nest would be a place for the robin to lay its eggs. What is a branch?",answer="A part of a tree that grows out from the trunk",hint="Reread the passage and look for words that support your answer.",explanation="The nest rests on a part of the tree.",choices={"A kind of bird food","A part of a tree that grows out from the trunk","A deep hole in soil","A baby robin"},tier="star-fallback",sourceFact="Original Grade 2 STAR-style practice",provenance={["kind"]="original-star-style"},priority=1},
    {id="original-star-103",subject="Reading / ELA",skill="Problem and solution",prompt="Read the passage: Sam wanted to read, but his little brother was playing a loud drum. Sam asked him to play in another room. His brother agreed. Sam smiled and opened his book. What problem did Sam have?",answer="The drum was too loud for reading",hint="Reread the passage and look for words that support your answer.",explanation="The loud drum interrupted the quiet he needed.",choices={"His book was wet","He lost his drum","The drum was too loud for reading","The room was dark"},tier="star-fallback",sourceFact="Original Grade 2 STAR-style practice",provenance={["kind"]="original-star-style"},priority=1},
    {id="original-star-104",subject="Reading / ELA",skill="Details",prompt="Read the passage: Sam wanted to read, but his little brother was playing a loud drum. Sam asked him to play in another room. His brother agreed. Sam smiled and opened his book. How did Sam solve the problem?",answer="He asked his brother to play elsewhere",hint="Reread the passage and look for words that support your answer.",explanation="Sam asked his brother to use another room.",choices={"He threw away the drum","He tore his book","He turned off a light","He asked his brother to play elsewhere"},tier="star-fallback",sourceFact="Original Grade 2 STAR-style practice",provenance={["kind"]="original-star-style"},priority=1},
    {id="original-star-105",subject="Reading / ELA",skill="Inference",prompt="Read the passage: Sam wanted to read, but his little brother was playing a loud drum. Sam asked him to play in another room. His brother agreed. Sam smiled and opened his book. How did Sam probably feel at the end?",answer="Pleased",hint="Reread the passage and look for words that support your answer.",explanation="Sam smiled and began reading after his brother agreed.",choices={"Pleased","Terrified","Angry at the book","Confused about the drum"},tier="star-fallback",sourceFact="Original Grade 2 STAR-style practice",provenance={["kind"]="original-star-style"},priority=1},
    {id="original-star-106",subject="Reading / ELA",skill="Sequence",prompt="Read the passage: Sam wanted to read, but his little brother was playing a loud drum. Sam asked him to play in another room. His brother agreed. Sam smiled and opened his book. What happened last?",answer="Sam opened his book",hint="Reread the passage and look for words that support your answer.",explanation="Opening the book is the final action.",choices={"The brother played loudly","Sam opened his book","Sam asked for a change","The brother agreed"},tier="star-fallback",sourceFact="Original Grade 2 STAR-style practice",provenance={["kind"]="original-star-style"},priority=1},
    {id="original-star-107",subject="Reading / ELA",skill="Main idea",prompt="Read the passage: Bees visit flowers to collect nectar. As they move, pollen sticks to their bodies. Some pollen rubs off on the next flower. Moving pollen between flowers helps many plants make seeds. What is the passage mainly explaining?",answer="How bees help plants",hint="Reread the passage and look for words that support your answer.",explanation="The passage explains how bees move pollen and help seed production.",choices={"How to draw a bee","Why flowers need snow","How bees help plants","Where bears sleep"},tier="star-fallback",sourceFact="Original Grade 2 STAR-style practice",provenance={["kind"]="original-star-style"},priority=1},
    {id="original-star-108",subject="Reading / ELA",skill="Details",prompt="Read the passage: Bees visit flowers to collect nectar. As they move, pollen sticks to their bodies. Some pollen rubs off on the next flower. Moving pollen between flowers helps many plants make seeds. What do bees collect from flowers?",answer="Nectar",hint="Reread the passage and look for words that support your answer.",explanation="The first sentence says they collect nectar.",choices={"Sand","Salt","Stones","Nectar"},tier="star-fallback",sourceFact="Original Grade 2 STAR-style practice",provenance={["kind"]="original-star-style"},priority=1},
